* t44evunlk.a -- CONF68K test t44: once the use count reaches zero, the event* is still there to be deleted.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): the other half of t43. Ev$Delet deletes "an event* from the system event table, freeing the entry for use by another event",* and may do so once the use count is zero (page 1-21).  Ev$Creat sets the* count to one, so one Ev$UnLnk brings it to zero and the delete must then* succeed, reporting no error.** THIS TEST EXISTS BECAUSE THE MANUAL CONTRADICTS ITSELF, and it is written to* make a real system settle the question rather than to confirm a guess.** Ev$UnLnk (page 1-20) says the use count is decremented "and the event is* deleted when the count reaches zero".  Read literally, the Ev$UnLnk below* deletes the event, and the Ev$Delet after it finds nothing and reports* E$EvNF (168).  Read the other way -- the count is bookkeeping and Ev$Delet* is what frees the entry -- the delete succeeds and reports 0.  Both readings* cannot be right, and the two answers are different numbers, so this test* tells them apart on whatever system runs it.** The expectation recorded here is 0, for reasons argued in claims.md and in* the comment on evDelet in the emulator's own source: the Ev$Delet page, the* OS-9 Guru and OS-9 Insights all describe delete-at-zero as a separate call,* and the literal reading would leave Ev$Delet unreachable by any program.* That is a reading of three sources, two of which are not Microware.  A FAIL* here reporting 168 is therefore not necessarily a defect in the system under* test -- it may be this suite that is wrong, and it is the single most* valuable line this suite could get back from real OS-9/68k hardware.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1FEvent set $53EvUnLnk set 1EvCreat set 2EvDelet set 3*INITVAL set 77EXPECT set 0* psect t44evunlk,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,2048,startstart lea evname(pc),a0 move.l #INITVAL,d0 move.w #EvCreat,d1 move.w #0,d2 move.w #1,d3 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcs.w setuperr move.l d0,d5** Count one to zero.  A failure HERE is a setup error and not a verdict: the* test has not yet reached the thing it is about. move.l d5,d0 move.w #EvUnLnk,d1 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcs.w setuperr** The delete this test is about. lea evname(pc),a0 move.w #EvDelet,d1 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcc.s deleted moveq #0,d6 move.w d1,d6 bra.s verdictdeleted moveq #0,d6verdict cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.w ispass bra.w isfail* use verdict.i use report.i*evname dc.b "cf44ev",0idstr dc.b "RESULT t44 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  Ev$Delet succeeds once the use count has reached zero",0 ends